<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cape Palmas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cape <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palmas</a> is a headland at the south-eastern end of Liberia, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Côte d'Ivoire</a>, where the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> turns east into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guinea">Gulf of Guinea</a>. In 1834 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland-state-colonization-society">Maryland State Colonization Society</a> founded a settlement there, which became the independent Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> in 1854 and joined Liberia in 1857. The town of Harper stands on the cape.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cape-palmas.jpg" alt="Cape Palmas" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wagner &amp; C., Lith., Philadelphia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cape_Palmas_etch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
